   "source": [
    " # AgentCore Memory Resource Management Operations\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates comprehensive **AgentCore Memory** lifecycle management using the AgentCoreMemoryProviderController.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What You'll Learn\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Create**: Memory providers with configurable retention\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Read**: Get memory provider details and configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Update**: Modify memory provider settings\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Delete**: Clean up memory provider resources\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Events**: Create and manage memory events\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Retrieve Memory Records**: List and retrieve memory records\n",
    "\n",
    "## AgentCore Memory Operations\n",
    "\n",
    "You can find boto3 (Python) AgentCore control plane memory provider operations on this page:\n",
    "\n",
    "https://boto3.amazonaws.com/v1/documentation/api/latest/reference/services/bedrock-agentcore-control.html\n",
    "\n",
    "* Note that AgentCore uses the term \"Memory\" for a memory provider that can have multiple memory strategies (semantic, summary, and user preferences) and can extract long-term memories from events after users or agents use the SDK call `create_event`. \n",
    "\n",
    "* The classes provided here under `src/agentic_platform/service/agentcore/memory\" wrap the AgentCore SDK service calls and attempt to disambiguate and refer to \"memory providers\" and \"memory events\" instead of \"memories\" and \"events,\" respectively.\n",
    "\n",
    "* The goal of the AgentCore support in this project is to demonstrate how to wrap those AgentCore calls in resource management services and deploy those resource management services to AWS via Terraform. \n",
    "\n",
    "* The memory provider operations there include:\n",
    "\n",
    "    * create_memory: note this is not a single memory event but a memory provider.\n",
    "\n",
    "    * get_memory: get information about a memory provider by memoryId\n",
    "\n",
    "    * delete_memory: delete the memory provider, not just a single memory event.\n",
    "\n",
    "    * list_memories: list memory providers, not memory events.\n",
    "\n",
    "    * update_memory: update a memory provider.\n",
    "\n",
    "You can find boto3 (Python) AgentCore data plane memory provider operations on this page:\n",
    "\n",
    "https://boto3.amazonaws.com/v1/documentation/api/latest/reference/services/bedrock-agentcore.html\n",
    "\n",
    "* The data plane memory provider operations include:\n",
    "\n",
    "    * create_event: create a single session memory event from the conversation session. For example, the agent may be instructed to create_event with the user's input and the model's output and thoughts in JSON format.\n",
    "\n",
    "    * delete_event: delete a single session memory event from the conversation session.\n",
    "\n",
    "    * get_event: get a single session memory event.\n",
    "\n",
    "    * list_event: update a single session memory event.\n",
    "\n",
    "    (note there's no update memory event)\n",
    "\n",
    "The example AgentCoreMemoryProviderController in this project currently supports these operations (more coverage to come):\n",
    "\n",
    "- `CREATE` - Create new memory providers\n",
    "- `GET` - Retrieve memory provider details\n",
    "- `UPDATE` - Update memory provider configurations\n",
    "- `DELETE` - Delete memory provider resources\n",
    "- `LIST_MEMORY_PROVIDERS` - List all memory providers\n",
    "- `CREATE_EVENT` - Create memory events\n",
    "- `LIST_EVENTS` - List memory events\n",
    "- `LIST_MEMORY_RECORDS` - List memory records\n",
    "- `WAIT_FOR_CREATE` - Wait for memory provider creation\n",
    "- `WAIT_FOR_DELETE` - Wait for memory provider deletion\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Concepts\n",
    "\n",
    "**AgentCore Memory**: A resource that can manage short-term and one or more long term memory strategies for agents and users. In this project, to disambiguate between memory and individual events (what people would call \"memories\") we refer to AgentCore Memory (or Memories plural, as in list_memories) as \"memory providers.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "**Memory Events**: Individual pieces of information stored in memory. AgentCore refers to these as events. They are short-term memories stored, which will be automatically converted to long-term memories according to the memory strategies configured for the memory provider.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Event Expiry**: Configurable retention period (minimum 7 days)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Memory Records**: Processed long-term memory data for retrieval. Can by of type semantic, summary, or user preference.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Prerequisites\n",
    "\n",
    "- AWS credentials with AgentCore permissions\n"
   ]
  },
